            <ArticleTitle>The influence of diabetes mellitus and obesity on upper limb arthroplasty outcomes: a systematic review protocol.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>3-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.11124/JBISRIR-2016-002940</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="REVIEW QUESTION/OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="UNASSIGNED">The objective of this review is to locate and synthesize the best available evidence investigating the impact of selected comorbidities on upper limb arthroplasty outcomes.The review question is: Are patients with diabetes mellitus or obesity at an increased risk of complications and/or poorer postoperative outcomes following total shoulder, reverse total shoulder and total elbow arthroplasty?</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
